{
  "title": [
    "midi.out"
  ],
  "description": "send MIDI data",
  "origin": "ELSE",
  "categories": [
    "MIDI"
  ],
  "inlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "anything",
          "description": "cooked MIDI data"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "float",
          "description": "MIDI channel"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "outlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "float",
          "description": "raw MIDI data"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "arguments": [
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "MIDI channel (0 is OMNI)",
      "default": "0"
    }
  ],
  "flags": [
    {
      "name": "-ext",
      "description": "only output to outlet"
    }
  ],
  "methods": [
    {
      "type": "ext <float>",
      "description": "non zero sets to listen only to external mode"
    }
  ],
  "body": "[midi.in] sends MIDI data from \"cooked\" data, instead of \"raw\" data like [midiout]. It takes data type symbol, values and channel (but a note output is received as a simple numeric list). It outputs raw MIDI data but it also sends out to the connected MIDI device."
}
